        }
      ],
      "assistant_text": "Now I understand the situation. The existing page is a stub on retrieval patterns. The source provides detailed, concrete information about hybrid retrieval\u2014a specific instantiation of retrieval patterns that combines sparse and dense search methods. This is clearly an update: the source enriches the existing page with specific techniques, their benefits, and production prevalence.\n\nI\u0027ll update the \u0060concepts/retrieval-patterns.md\u0060 page to integrate this source content. The source mentions:\n- Hybrid retrieval specifically (combines BM25 \u002B dense vectors)\n- Reciprocal rank fusion as the merging mechanism\n- Performance advantages (outperforms either method alone)\n- Real-world applicability (default in production RAG systems)\n- Use cases (queries with rare identifiers \u002B natural language)\n\nLet me update the page and then update the index with a revised description:",
